      "title": "Hear about jobs that are right for you?Sign up for job alerts",
      "description": "Student Aide Programmer - Fredericksburg, Virginia, United States Applicant Login About UMW Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion Aspire Org Chart Map Benefits Benefits for Faculty Medical / Health Insurance Leave Holidays Resources for Applicants FAQ Contact Us Search Jobs Using PUP Compensation Estimator Resources for Current Employees Hiring Compensation Using PUP Kiosk mode Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Student Aide Programmer Fredericksburg, Virginia, United States, 22401 Student Employee Add to favorites View favorites Title: Student Aide Programmer VP Area: Chief of Staff - UMW Department: Information Technology Campus Location: Main Campus Advertised Range: $13.00 per hour Job Summary/Basic Functions Under direct supervision, the Student Aide will develop reports, assist with web interfaces and provide general database maintenance that helps the Enterprise Applications team support the reporting and programming requirements of the University. Required KSAs/Competencies/Qualifications Current UMW sophomores/rising juniors in all degrees, with a demonstrated proficiency in programming logic. While the student may not already have substantial computer science classwork or knowledge, the hope is they will grow and learn in the position and be able to apply their skills from their coursework in a positive and collaborative manner throughout their academic career at the University of Mary Washington. Required Experience: Experience with programming logic or relational databases is preferred. Required Education: Current UMW sophomores/rising juniors in all degrees, with a demonstrated proficiency in programming logic. Required Licensure: N/A Additional Considerations: Special Instructions You will be provided a confirmation of receipt when your application and/or résumé is submitted successfully. Please refer to “Your Application” in your account to check the status of your application for this position. To be considered for this position a state application must be received through the online employment system at https://jobs.umw.edu/ . Mailed, emailed, faxed, or hand-delivered applications or resumes will not be accepted. Excluding current UMW employees, selected candidate(s) must successfully pass a criminal history background check. Employment verification will be conducted to include current/previous supervisory employment reference checks. Other financial, credit, driving, background checks or completion of Statement of Economic Interests may be required for certain positions. For more information, please visit http://ethics.dls.virginia.gov/ . The University of Mary Washington adheres to the principle of equal opportunity. The University does not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, sex, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, parental status (including pregnancy), national origin, age, disability, family medical history or genetic information, political affiliation, military service, or other non-merit based factors in recruiting, admitting, enrolling students or hiring and promoting faculty and staff members. Complaints of discrimination should be directed to the EEO officer of the University. UMW Values Veterans: UMW is a proud member of the Commonwealth of Virginia Values Veterans (V3) Program, authorized under the Code of Virginia (§2.2-2001.2). We are committed to recruiting, hiring, and retaining qualified Veterans and their spouses. Veterans who are hired into state positions may be eligible for additional leave accruals based on their total years of service in the military, National Guard or Reserve. For more information please visit: https://www.dhrm.virginia.gov/employeebenefits . In support of the Commonwealth’s commitment to inclusion, we are encouraging individuals with disabilities to apply through the Commonwealth Alternative Hiring Process (AHP). To be considered for this opportunity, applicants will need to provide their AHP Letter (formerly Certificate of Disability or COD) provided by the Department for Aging & Rehabilitative Services (DARS) or the Department for the Blind & Vision Impaired (DBVI). Service-Connected Veterans are encouraged to answer Veteran status questions and submit their disability documentation, if applicable, to DARS/DBVI to get their AHP Letter. Requesting an AHP Letter can be found at AHP Letter or by calling DARS at 800-552-5019. Note: Applicants who received a Certificate of Disability from DARS or DBVI dated between April 1, 2022- February 29, 2024, can still use that COD as applicable documentation for the Alternative Hiring Process. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 698d48f0 Last Name (required) 35288b34 Email (required) 78aa326a Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Financial Aid Peer Counselor Fredericksburg, Virginia, United States, 22401 Admissions Responsibilities include receiving and answering basic financial aid-related questions for incoming customers via telephone, e-mail, and front desk reception; intelligently explaining to customers basic information about Federal Student Aid programs and processes; providing excellent customer service while maintaining confidentiality of students’ records appropriate to FERPA regulations; working closely with the Financial Aid Customer Service Team. Student Facility Assistant Fredericksburg, Virginia, United States, 22401 Facilities Operations Help UMW Grounds keep campus beautiful! Collect recycling and trash from cans and toters around campus. Must be comfortable driving a university truck around campus. Must complete UMW Van Familiarization before starting. Senior Accountant Fredericksburg, Virginia, United States, 22401 Finance This position supports the financial operations of the institution by independently performing complex accounting and reconciliation functions in accordance with institutional policies, state and federal regulations, and generally accepted accounting principles (GAAP). STARS Ambassador - Center for STARS Fredericksburg, Virginia, United States, 22401 Registrar's Office The Center for STARS is seeking hardworking, organized, and self-motivated students to serve as STARS Ambassadors. Ambassadors assist with office operations, help plan events, and represent STARS at campus and community programs. This role provides an opportunity to connect with prospective and current students, share your UMW experience, and serve as a positive representative of the university. Grounds Lead Worker Fredericksburg, Virginia, United States, 22401 Grounds Support the Landscape & Grounds mission of maintaining the UMW landscape & grounds in a safe, neat, clean and aesthetically pleasing manner. The UMW Landscape & Grounds Department strives to provide exceptional service and a safe environment to the UMW community and visitors, while being an environmental steward in maintaining a beautiful and inviting university. Contracts & Resourcing Manager Fredericksburg, Virginia, United States, 22401 Capital Outlay The University of Mary Washington has an exciting opportunity to join our team as a Contracts & Resourcing Manager. Hear about jobs that are right for you? Sign up for job alerts Job Alert a44b8e68 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Information Technology Information Technology Categories Student Employment Student Employment Employment Type Student Employee Student Employee First Name (required) 1834da6b Last Name (required) 392dd6c0 Email (required) 078e01f0 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Terms & Conditions Privacy Policy Candidate Details Please choose the employment type(s)"
