    "https://jobs.umw.edu/jobs/contracts-resourcing-manager-fredericksburg-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Hear about jobs that are right for you?Sign up for job alerts",
      "description": "Contracts & Resourcing Manager - Fredericksburg, Virginia, United States Applicant Login About UMW Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion Aspire Org Chart Map Benefits Benefits for Faculty Medical / Health Insurance Leave Holidays Resources for Applicants FAQ Contact Us Search Jobs Using PUP Compensation Estimator Resources for Current Employees Hiring Compensation Using PUP Kiosk mode Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Contracts & Resourcing Manager Fredericksburg, Virginia, United States, 22401 Full Time Closing on: Oct 11 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Title: Contracts & Resourcing Manager VP Area: Administration & Finance - UMW Department: Capital Outlay Campus Location: Main Campus Advertised Range: $53,000 - $55,167 (A final salary offer will be determined by the selected candidate's qualifications, and is not is not negotiable beyond what is advertised.) Job Summary/Basic Functions The University of Mary Washington has an exciting opportunity to join our team as a Contracts & Resourcing Manager. In this role, you will provide support, coordination, and direction regarding capital outlay, maintenance reserve, and non-capital construction project procurement, records management, reporting, and records retention for the University. Provide coordination and manage assigned departmental processes and responsibilities. The State and Local Government Conflict of Interests Act requires specific officers and employees of the Commonwealth of Virginia to file written disclosure statements, Statement of Economic Interests (SOEI), of their financial interests annually. This position has been designated as a covered position and the selected candidate will be required to file the SOEI disclosure by the first day of employment. Required KSAs/Competencies/Qualifications Demonstrated experience in administrative and financial responsibility in a large organization and/or government agency. Substantial knowledge, skill and ability in facilities related recordkeeping including public procurement practices. Ability to perform high level administrative support in a higher education environment. Significant computer expertise with knowledge of Microsoft Office applications, Adobe products, website publishing, electronic procurement systems and/or other automated office tools. Strong writing, proofreading and editing skills. Excellent organizational, communication, and customer service skills with the ability to meet deadlines and manage multiple tasks simultaneously. Knowledge regarding public procurement best practices and the DGS central electronic procurement website. Required Experience: Experience in Facilities and Capital Outlay Administration and/or public sector procurement in a higher education or government agency environment. Required Education: N/A Required Licensure: Certification as a Virginia Contracting Officer (VCO) and/or Virginia Construction Contracting Officer (VCCO) or the ability to gain certification within twelve to eighteen months of employment. Additional Considerations: KSAs: Budget management, purchasing rules, FOIA, SWaM and Micro-Vendor requirements, and human resource management skills. EDUCATION: Completion of a college degree from an accredited college/university in a related field or equivalent training and experience. Experience: Previous experience working in higher education facilities administration, facilities administration, and Virginia State Agency. LICENSURE/CERTIFICATION: Current or past certification as a VCA, VCO, VCCO, or other procurement certification. Special Instructions You will be provided a confirmation of receipt when your application and/or résumé is submitted successfully. Please refer to “Your Application” in your account to check the status of your application for this position. To be considered for this position a state application must be received through the online employment system at https://jobs.umw.edu/ . Mailed